In this module, I explored how to manage and interact with Windows systems through the Command Prompt. 
I learned how to retrieve system information using commands such as ver and systeminfo, as well as check network configurations with ipconfig, ping, tracert,
nslookup, and netstat.

I also practiced navigating directories and managing files using commands like cd, dir, tree, mkdir, rmdir, type, copy, move, and del. 
These exercises helped me understand how to perform everyday file management tasks directly through the command line.

Another important part of the module focused on process management. I learned how to list running processes with tasklist, filter results, 
and terminate specific processes using taskkill and their process IDs (PIDs). I also explored system power commands, including shutdown /r, shutdown /s, 
and shutdown /a to restart, shut down, or cancel a scheduled shutdown.

This module improved my confidence using the Windows Command Prompt and strengthened my understanding of system administration, network troubleshooting, 
and process management, which are useful skills in Cybersecurity.
